7. USERS, ROLES, AND PERMISSIONS

Design a simple initial permission system.

Suggested roles:

Diamond Platform Administrator

- Manages the software platform and authorized platform-level operations.
- Has no unrestricted access to customer business data by default.
- Any exceptional support access must be controlled and audited.

Business Owner

- Manages their own business workspace.
- Invites employees and manages their permissions.
- Configures business settings and views authorized business information.

Business Manager

- Manages permitted operational functions and team activities.

Employee

- Uses only assigned or otherwise authorized features and records.

Read-Only User

- Can view authorized information without modifying it.

Enforce these permissions in backend policies and application logic. Hiding a menu item is not a security control.

Document every permission and test both allowed and forbidden actions.

